^{:go/end 1061} (go/method bytes "bytes writes the value of z into buf using big-endian encoding.\nThe value of z is encoded in the slice buf[i:]. If the value of z\ncannot be represented in buf, bytes panics. The number i of unused\nbytes at the beginning of buf is returned as result.\n" [^nat z ^{:tag (slice byte)} buf] :results [^int i]
  ;; This function is used in cryptographic operations. It must not leak
  ;; anything but the Int's sign and bit size through side-channels. Any
  ;; changes must be reviewed by a security expert.
  (set! i (len buf))
  (range [_ d z]
    (for [j 0] (< j _S) (inc! j)
      (dec! i)
      (cond (>= i 0)
        (aset buf i (conv byte d))
        (!= (conv byte d) 0)
